<title>CANADA: TENNIS-QUEBEC CITY WOMEN'S RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-QUEBEC CITY WOMEN'S RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>QUEBEC CITY 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the $164,250</p>
<p>Bell Challenge women's tennis tournament on Wednesday (Prefix</p>
<p>number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>First round</p>
<p>1-Brenda Schultz-McCarthy (Netherlands) beat Stephanie De</p>
<p>Ville (Belgium) 7-6 (7-3) 6-2</p>
<p>Nicole Arendt (U.S.) beat Rene Simpson (Canada) 6-0 6-7 (5-7)</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>Els Callens (Belgium) beat 3-Amy Frazier (U.S.) 3-6 6-2 6-4</p>
<p>5-Lisa Raymond (U.S.) beat Debbie Graham (U.S.) 7-5 6-2</p>
<p>6-Florencia Labat (Argentina) beat Patricia Hy-Boulais</p>
<p>(Canada) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Tami Whitlinger-Jones (U.S.) beat Jana Nejedly (Canada) 3-6</p>
<p>7-6 (7-2) 6-4</p>
</text>
